FSR / fp_exception subtype tests, beyond floating_point/invalid_ops/ (which
only covers the invalid-operation case).

- accrued_inexact.s : the FSR's aexc (sticky, accrued) vs cexc (current op
  only) distinction, per the manual's FSR conformance requirement. Asserts
  our own model's behavior directly against the manual (see
  compliance/README.md Issue 1 for the fuller writeup and the AJIT-diff
  evidence this formalizes).
- overflow.s / underflow.s / division_by_zero.s : IEEE-754 overflow,
  underflow, and division-by-zero, each with its own FSR trap-enable bit
  set, asserting FSR.cexc after the resulting fp_exception trap is exactly
  the single expected bit (per Appendix C.7's
  "cexc <- most_significant_bit_of(texc and TEM)").

Not testable given this implementation's design (see model/cpp_common_code/
SparcCore.cpp): unfinished_FPop and unimplemented_FPop are both
architecturally unreachable here -- FPops execute synchronously
(fpu_c is always set before complete_fp_execution checks it) and the FPU is
always present (bp_FPU_present hardwired 1), so neither condition can ever
be true.
